# Project context

Build a React + TypeScript chat UI that sends and displays messages from all authors, resembling the mockups in `../frontend-engineer/assets/`. Wire to `../frontend-challenge-chat-api` (do not modify that repo).

## Challenge requirements

- Timebox mindset: prefer a solid core path over extras (brief: ~4–6 hours).
- Technology: React + TypeScript (Vite SPA). Do not introduce Next.js.
- Responsiveness: common browsers + mobile.
- Code quality: readable code, frequent useful commits, performance and accessibility prioritized.

## What reviewers look for

- Code readability and clean architecture
- Commit quality (frequent, descriptive)
- Fast load / efficient mobile rendering
- Accessibility
- Design attention (not pixel-perfect; detail matters)

## API facts

- Base URL and token from env (`VITE_API_BASE_URL`, `VITE_API_TOKEN`).
- Bearer auth on message endpoints.
- `GET /api/v1/messages` and `POST /api/v1/messages` only — no WebSocket; poll with `?after=`.
- Default list order from API is oldest-first; trust the live API over brief wording.

## Out of scope unless explicitly requested

- Editing the API repo, auth UI, edit/delete messages, inventing realtime transports.
